# a comment line may open the file, before the description
> Every construct the .bs grammar accepts, gathered in one document.
> The description may run over several lines.

name Exhaustive
slug bookshelf-exhaustive
version 5.0.0
tags runtime, datapack-only
weak_dependencies bs.log, bs.block
documentation https://docs.mcbookshelf.dev/en/latest/modules/exhaustive.html
authors Aksiome, Leirof
contributors theogiraudet
since 2022/04/14 1.18.2

# a comment between the definitions, at any indentation
  # and indented
$block: #[id="block"] string > a type, attributed
$block_state: $block | struct > a type holding a struct: its fields follow
  id: $block > a type used inside another
  properties?: #[as=mcdoc:block_states[[id]]] struct > an attribute with nested brackets, and an empty struct
$ratio: double @ 0..1
> a doc on the next line
$open: number @ 0<..<1 > a '<' on a side excludes that bound
$position:
  > a struct: fields indented under the name, the doc as the first line of the block
  x: int
  y: int
  z: int
$every:
  whole: int
  tiny: byte
  small: short
  big: long
  single: float @ 0.5..1.
  wide: double @ ..2.5
  above: number @ 0<..
  below: number @ ..<1
  loose: number @ -1..1
  text: string @ 1..
  flag: boolean
  anything: any
  compound: struct
  ints: int[] @ 4
  bytes: byte @ 0..1 [] @ 1..
  longs: long[] @ ..8
  names: [string] @ 2
  rows: [struct] @ 1..3 > a list of structs
    cell: int
  pair: [int, string]
  lone: [int,]
  either: int | string > a union
  nested:
    leaf:
    > a doc on the next line, before the block
      depth: short
  maybe?: boolean
  aliased: $block
  state: $block_state
  ratio: $ratio | $open
  attributed: #[id="item"] string
  merged: #[id="item"] $block > an attribute merged onto the type
  function: string > a field named after a language word
  storage: int
  since: int
  input: int
  struct: struct
  int: int
  1: int > a number as a name
  $position
$done:
  output state > lines, pasted in a feature
$shared:
  contributors Bafy78
  @position > a position, with its default type
  input storage bs.exhaustive:shared payload/levels: > a storage with its own target and path
    levels: int
  $done

$face[bottom, top]
$flag[1, 2, 4]
$axis[x]:
  nth: first
  since: 2025/01/25 1.21.4
$axis[y, z]:
  nth: another, a text running to the end of its line: colons, > and # included
  since: 2025/05/14 1.21.5

feature function add_levels
  > A feature doc as the first line of the block.
  authors Aksiome
  contributors Leirof
  since 2022/04/14 1.18.2
  deprecated
  experimental

  @executor: player | entity > an executor takes players and entities
  @position: xyz
  > a doc on the next line
  @rotation: xy
  @dimension: overworld | nether | end | any
  @state > a condition the world must meet
  input arguments:
    levels: int @ 0..
  input storage in:
    extra?: $every
  input state
  output storage: int[] @ 3 > a Minecraft array, bounded in size
  output result: int
  output success
  output state > every line of a feature

feature function bs.exhaustive:set_levels > A feature id written with its namespace.
  @executor: entity[] > an array of entities
  input macro:
    levels: int > a hand-written macro
  $shared

feature function has_levels > The same name as the predicate below: another registry, so allowed.
  input arguments: $position
  output storage: $every

feature predicate has_levels
> A feature doc on the next line.
  @executor: player
  input storage:
    whole: int
  output success > whether the player has levels

feature loot_table roll_levels > The contexts with their default types.
  @executor
  @position
  @rotation
  @dimension
  input state
  output state

feature context_int_provider level_count > A registry holding underscores.
  input storage:
    count: int
  output result: int @ 0..

feature context_float_provider $axis/ratio > Get the $axis ratio, the $axis.nth one: a feature repeated over a list.
  since $axis.since
  @position: entity
  output result: float > the $axis ratio

feature predicate face/$face/$flag > Check the $face face against the flag `$flag`: every combination exists.
  output success

feature block_tag can_occlude > A block tag declares no line but metadata.

feature entity_type_tag is_mob > An entity type tag declares no line either.

feature structure oak/1 > The last registry: a structure.
# a trailing comment line
